# Typed refusals

> This file is GENERATED from `ontology.ttl` and must not be edited. Change the
> ontology or `templates/typed_refusals.md.tmpl`, then regenerate.

Every `{:error, _}` this library returns carries an `AshGraphLaw.Refusal` with a
closed `code`, a closed `class`, and the Chatman failure-taxonomy `broken_term` the
refusal witnesses. A refusal is an observation about one exact input. GraphLaw
derives and validates; it never authorizes, so a refusal neither grants nor
withdraws authority.

Every refusal also carries `:raw`: the whole engine error map exactly as decoded, so
fields this library does not know survive unchanged. It is `nil` for client-side refusals
built with `AshGraphLaw.Refusal.new/3`, `AshGraphLaw.Refusal.build/3` or a per-code
constructor. `build/3` takes a required message and raises `ArgumentError` for a code
outside the closed table.

The capability codes `invalid_capability_request`, `unknown_capability`,
`capability_not_declared`, `capability_parity_drift` and `capability_response_undecodable`
(orders 36 to 40) are client-side: they are raised by the typed capability surface, never
by the engine.

